			"date": "2024-05-09T15:12:15.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@asci\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>asci</span></a></span> have you used any framework besides react? You know they've all solved these problems without jsx right? You may be making some assumptions about what I'm saying. I'm not suggesting that template literals is a complete solution. I am saying that if we had template strings, the solution would've been simpler and more compatible with JavaScript.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
