			"date": "2024-05-10T06:28:19.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://social.polotek.net/@polotek\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>polotek</span></a></span> yea, I’ve been using Backbone (also w/ Marionette), Knockout and a bit of Angular. They all suffered from rigid composition issues with templates. I also tried Solid, but with manually manipulating DOM elements (may not be the best practice, it was an interview requirement) and had a side project on Elm. I not saying that it is not possible to make good solution using templates strings, but I can’t imagine that. An example may help, otherwise it seems like a hot take</p>",
